          "Lead on workforce and economic development with specificity: the 18.8% college attainment rate is the sharpest economic vulnerability in this district's data, and policies that expand vocational training, trade credentialing, and employer investment in northwestern Louisiana speak directly to both the white working-class majority and Black working families simultaneously.",
          "Engage rural healthcare and aging-population services as the primary quality-of-life agenda — the 44.3 median age and $53,088 income together describe a constituency approaching retirement age without significant financial cushion, for whom hospital access, Medicare sustainability, and long-term care availability are the most consequential government decisions.",
          "Do not mistake the 66% margin for an invitation to govern passively — a landslide result in a low-college-attainment, moderate-income district is often the product of candidate quality and turnout dynamics as much as durable alignment, and any future cycle that produces a credible challenger with strong Black community mobilization and economic-anxiety messaging among white working-class voters can move this margin faster than the 2023 result suggests."
