          "Invest heavily in ward- and block-level Black voter mobilization — at 64.24% Black, the district's Democratic ceiling is high enough to win decisively, but a 52% result suggests turnout gaps or persuasion losses that a disciplined ground operation and authentic community presence can close before the next cycle.",
