        memoHeadline: "Uncontested but Not Invulnerable: A 75% Black, Low-Income, Majority-Renter District Where the Real Electoral Work Happens Before the General Ballot",
        memoParagraphs: [
          "LA-HD-3 is, by its 2023 general election result, uncontested territory — Representative Phelps ran unopposed and received 100% of the vote. But the absence of opposition on the general election ballot is not evidence of political security; it is evidence that the competitive arena for this seat is the Democratic primary, where turnout among a deeply engaged Black constituency at $34,734 median income will determine who holds power. The district's demographic profile is among the most racially concentrated in any Louisiana legislative district: 75.8% Black, 17% white, 4.13% Hispanic, 0.54% Asian, with a small residual gap likely representing American Indian or Alaska Native residents. At a median age of 33.8, this is a young constituency, and at 55.1% renter rate and $34,734 median household income, it is a constituency that lives the consequences of housing policy, wage stagnation, and public services delivery in direct and immediate ways.",
          "The 11.7% college attainment rate is the most strategically significant number in the district's profile — not because it reflects a failure of aspiration, but because it defines the communication environment and the policy agenda simultaneously. A constituency where fewer than 12 in 100 adults hold a college degree is a constituency that evaluates its representative not on legislative process fluency or abstract policy positioning but on whether conditions in the district are materially improving: whether rents are manageable, whether jobs pay enough to stay, whether schools and public safety and healthcare are present and functional. The 55.1% renter rate in a district with this income level signals a constituency under direct and ongoing housing cost pressure — and renters at this income level have limited buffers against displacement, cost increases, or landlord non-compliance. Any candidate who holds or seeks this seat must demonstrate, in concrete and specific terms, what they have done or will do about the material conditions of renting, working, and raising a family at the economic margins of one of the lower-income districts in Louisiana's legislature."
        ],
