          { name: "Climate and environmental regulation as primary economic driver", tag: "avoid", why: "A district with $55,063 median income and 28% renters is economically vulnerable and unlikely to prioritize environmental restrictions that threaten local jobs or raise energy/living costs. Green energy rhetoric disconnected from local job creation will read as elite and hostile to working families. Any environmental message must be paired explicitly with economic benefit or job preservation to avoid fatal credibility loss." }
