          { name: "Abstract Ideological Positioning Disconnected from Economic Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "A district with 15% college attainment, $46,464 median household income, and a 55% Black working-class constituency is evaluating its representative on concrete material outcomes — not on rhetorical alignment with either progressive ideology or centrist Democratic positioning. Legislative communications and campaign messaging built around abstract ideological framing rather than specific policy deliverables will register as disconnected from the material conditions of people who are managing tight household budgets, navigating the rental market, and looking for credentialed workforce pathways. The 81% mandate was extended by a constituency with specific economic needs, and the representative who holds that mandate most durably is the one who can point to concrete wins on healthcare, jobs, and housing — not the one with the most ideologically coherent brand profile." }
