          "Address housing cost and renter affordability as a first-tier economic issue — a 33.2% renter rate in a $78K median income district signals real cost pressure that the headline income figure masks, and ignoring it cedes the issue to any challenger who engages it.",
          "Leverage the 43.8% college-educated majority with policy-specific, competence-forward communication — this is a constituency that responds to demonstrated expertise and concrete legislative accomplishment, not generic partisan positioning."
