          "Define constituent service as the primary electoral defense: in an unopposed district, the threat to incumbency comes from primary challengers who can credibly argue the representative is not delivering — answer that argument preemptively with a visible, specific legislative record on economic issues.",
          "Engage workforce development and wage policy with specificity for non-college adults — the 28% college attainment rate means a majority of working-age residents in this district depend on job training pipelines, employer accountability, and labor market access that does not require a degree to navigate.",
          "Avoid the complacency of an uncontested margin — 100% of the vote in an unopposed race is not a mandate; it is a placeholder that disappears the moment a credible primary challenger emerges with a sharper record on housing, wages, or public investment in the district."
