          { name: "Treating 56% as a Durable Majority", tag: "avoid", why: "A 56-44 result in a majority-minority district at $79,231 income is not a safe seat — it is a persuadable seat whose margin is contingent on specific turnout and coalition conditions that could shift materially in a higher-salience election cycle. The demographic arithmetic of HD-105 means that a candidate who consolidates only the existing coalition without actively managing the Black community's mobilization level, the Hispanic community's participation rate, and working-class renter concerns is holding a margin with no buffer. In Louisiana legislative races, 2023 special election dynamics — lower overall turnout, specific mobilization advantages — can produce results that overstate structural partisan alignment, and a candidate who campaigns the next cycle on the assumption that 56% reflects the district's natural center will be caught flat-footed." }
