          { name: "Single-Constituency Campaigning That Ignores Renter-Homeowner Tension", tag: "avoid", why: "With 40.7% renters and approximately 59% homeowners, LA-SD-16 has a built-in policy tension between constituencies whose material interests around housing, taxation, and development frequently diverge. A legislative record or campaign posture that consistently prioritizes homeowner interests — property value protection, limited development, property tax stability — at the expense of renter concerns will fracture a coalition that the unopposed result falsely implies is unified. At 36.3 median age and $80,277 income, neither renters nor homeowners in this district are operating from a position of economic ease, which means both groups are paying attention to whether policy delivers for them specifically. Ignoring this fault line until a challenger exploits it is the most avoidable strategic error available in this district." }
