          { name: "Abstract Partisan Messaging Disconnected from Local Economic Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "With 16.1% college attainment and a $51,072 median income, the district's voters are not primarily motivated by ideological or culture-war framing — they are motivated by whether government is making their material lives better or worse. Generic partisan messaging that does not translate into specific answers about healthcare costs, local jobs, and public services will fail to build the cross-demographic coalition a candidate needs when this seat eventually draws a competitive challenger. At this income level, voters who feel economically left behind will evaluate candidates on delivery, not affiliation, and a campaign that substitutes ideological positioning for specific local governance commitments leaves the economic-anxiety vote available for the opposition." }
