          "Address working-class white economic anxiety with specificity and local grounding: at $60,420 median income and 24.6% college attainment, the district's white majority is not ideologically sealed against a Democratic candidate who speaks directly to wages, utility costs, healthcare affordability, and job quality — these are the pressure points that make 38% Republican support a ceiling rather than a floor.",
          "Make housing cost and renter stability a signature issue: with 32.7% of residents renting at a working-class income level, rising rents and housing instability are direct material threats to a significant portion of the constituency — a candidate who owns this issue with concrete policy proposals builds loyalty among a bloc that is economically motivated but not strongly partisan-loyal.",
