          "Lead on working-class economic security: at $60,334 income with a 30.5% renter rate and 27% college attainment, the district's households are financially exposed to healthcare costs, housing instability, and wage stagnation — these are the pressure points where the 61% majority can fracture if a challenger offers concrete answers.",
          "Speak specifically to the young constituency: a 35.5-year median age means a large share of the electorate is in the early stages of career, family, and homeownership formation — education access, workforce development, and economic opportunity are not abstract; they are what this demographic is actively navigating right now.",
